Third-party references and attributions:

* SF Pro typeface. Copyright (c) Apple Inc.
  Not bundled. Referenced only via the `-apple-system` font fallback chain
  in colors_and_type.css. Renders natively on Apple hardware via the
  operating system; falls back to the local system font on other platforms.
  Apple distributes SF Pro at https://developer.apple.com/fonts/ under its
  own license terms.

* SF Symbols. Copyright (c) Apple Inc.
  Not bundled. This bundle substitutes SF Symbols glyphs with Lucide
  (https://lucide.dev/, ISC License) per the iconography mapping in
  bundle/preview/iconography.html. Lucide is loaded by reference from the
  public CDN at unpkg.com.

* Apple wallpapers and other Apple-owned imagery. **Not included** in this
  bundle. The previous releases referenced four Apple system wallpapers
  (Aurora, Sequoia, Ventura, Monterey) plus a cover background; all have
  been removed in v0.1.2 in favor of procedural CSS mesh gradients
  (the `--demo-backdrop` variable in colors_and_type.css and the four
  alternative gradients in bundle/preview/wallpapers.html). Those
  procedural gradients are pure CSS and are released under the same MIT
  terms as the rest of this software.

* Design tokens in bundle/colors_and_type.css. Calibrated against the
  public "macOS 26 (Community).fig" file from Apple Design Resources
  (https://www.figma.com/@apple). Individual numeric values (colors,
  radii, spacings, durations) are facts and not individually copyrightable;
  the curated token set is released under MIT.

* HTML specimens in bundle/preview/*.html and bundle/showcase.html. MIT.
  These are clean-room visual recreations of the macOS 26 UI patterns
  intended for design exploration, prototyping and instruction. They do
  not bundle any Apple-owned binary assets.

* This bundle was wrapped as an Agent Skill via Claude Design at
  https://claude.ai/design and follows the Anthropic Agent Skills 2.0
  specification at
  https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview.
